1) fix parameters in common.inc.sh if you want to

*******************************************************************************
COMPILING
*******************************************************************************

  ./make

*******************************************************************************
RUNNING
*******************************************************************************

There are three executables:

./target/release/src/iseql 
  that measures runtime only
./target/counters/src/iseql 
  that also provides output for counters
./target/ebi//src/iseql 
  that uses the ebi instead of lebi join

*******************************************************************************
USAGE
*******************************************************************************

./target/release/src/iseql <cmd> <relationR> <relationG> <disabledExperiments>
  where <cmd> can be:
    reverse-during
    start-preceding
    left-overlap
    before-join
    
  <relationR> and <relationG> can be:
    --file <file>
      load data from a tab separated file -- one interval of integers per line
    --uni <tuple count> <max tuple length>
      uses intervals with uniformly distributed duration and start points 
      specifying tuple count and max duration (domain is 1-1e6)
    --exp <tuple count> <avg tuple length>
      uses intervals with exponentially distributed duration and uniformly 
      distributed start points specifying tuple count and average duration 
      (domain is 1-1e6)
      
  <disabledExperiments> is used to specify a comma-separated list of disabled 
  approaches, e.g, "lm" disables the Leung-MuntzJoin. Use "" for all approaches
  enables.  
  
*******************************************************************************
EXAMPLE
******************************************************************************* 

The following provides the runtime in seconds and the number of result tuples 
for the start-preceding join for all approaches with relation R of size 1000 intervals with 
uniformly distributed durations and maximum duration of 100 and relation G of 
size 500 intervals with exponentially distributed durations and average 
duration of 50:

./target/release/src/iseql start-preceding --uni 1000 100 --exp 500 50 ""  
      